[#:seon.task{:name "a-deleted-functions-fault-never-resolves"
             :kind :function
             :intent "resolution needs the fault's function entity, so a fault naming a deleted function can never resolve: the seon.flow/release-admission! ClassCastException fault stays open after 69229772b deleted the function and its cause. Also faults whose operation never had a function entity: superv.async/throw-if-exception- (477a97dc, 67029fe7, 2026-09-27) can resolve only by resolve!. The wider rule is task seon.error/health-stays-faulted-on-dead-process-faults."
             :must-read #{seon.error/resolution}
             :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/stability-sweep-2026-09-27.md"
                         "docs/research/agent-platform/landing/inv-lifecycle-storage-opus-2026-09-26.md"
                         "docs/seon/issues/a-fault-whose-function-is-deleted-never-resolves.md"}}
 #:seon.task{:name "a-missing-key-message-reads-badly"
             :kind :function
             :intent "`seon.error/explain-problem` describes a missing key `[:map [:at inst?]]` as 'the required key :at with a value satisfying should be an inst', and an `:=` schema `[:= {:description \"d\"} true]` refusing false as 'a value satisfying should be true': the fallback in `seon.error/schema-expectation` puts Malli's own 'should be' sentence after 'a value satisfying'. Done when neither `:seon.error/expected-description` contains 'satisfying should' or 'with should', the missing one still names :at, and the `:=` one names true. The description comes from the schema, never by reading or trimming Malli's message text (root refused fan6-key's regex and fan7-key's 'should be ' prefix strip). Live instance (fan-out 7): `(my.program/diff {})` refused 'expected the required key :my.program/base-ctx with must be an SCI evaluation context'."
             :must-read #{seon.error/explain-problem seon.error/schema-expectation malli.error/error-message}
             :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/landing/error-text-2026-09-26.md"}}
 #:seon.task{:name "fault-observation-returns-the-recorded-error"
             :kind :function
             :intent "occurred-since returns each touched error's recorded observation with its references and resolution instead of a signature/message/count summary, and resolution never hides a fault from its window; for-agent reaches the escalation owner of a fault no steward answers for (audit §2.5 items 5-6)."
             :must-read #{seon.error/occurred-since seon.error/for-agent}
             :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/error-delivery-audit-2026-09-26.md"}}
 #:seon.task{:name "error-transactions-carry-references-never-worlds"
             :kind :function
             :intent "An error-recording transaction's writer call carried the whole schema projection, so any refused write copied it into its refusal and the operator could not read the failure back (owner 2026-09-26, start --head at 7c40396b3). The call holds data and references; the writer reads its database's own projection."
             :must-read #{seon.error/recording seon.error/commit-call}
             :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/landing/err-s3-fault-identity-opus-2026-09-26.md"}}
 #:seon.task{:name "refusal-html-reads-as-fragments"
             :kind :function
             :intent "Since ea802169d each shown value in a refusal's HTML is a block seon-data-panel mid-sentence, breaking the sentence; the sentence repeats the schema key after 'a string'; a missing key shows :seon.error/unknown as the offending value; the refusal path shows a raw entity id [56626 :my.plan.item/title]; a fault with no operation renders an empty seon-kicker paragraph. Values inline (a CSS rule for .seon-error-problem .seon-data-panel in resources/public/css/input.css), no repeated key, a missing key named as missing, no entity-id dump, no empty kicker; check browser paint (fix-html-views 1c10d3536)."
             :must-read #{seon.error/render-html}
             :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/red-triage-3-2026-09-27.md"}}
 #:seon.task{:name "health-stays-faulted-on-dead-process-faults"
             :kind :function
             :intent "At 18:01Z 2026-09-27 all 10 open faults came from dead processes and 7 were stale: resolution (error.clj ~1309-1354) fires only when the digest of `:seon.instrument/fn` changes, and that fn is often the reporter (memory-pressure-crossed!, record-write-refusal-fault!, `seon.maintenance/exception-value`) or an outer wrapper (`seon.test/run`'s digest change resolved three record-tx signatures while record-tx still refused; settle-batch-refusal! stays open after its cause was fixed elsewhere), or absent (superv.async; see seon.error/a-deleted-functions-fault-never-resolves). runtime_status reads :faulted whenever any fault is open. Let the producer's error schema declare process scope (e.g. memory pressure, the write-refusal park, a stop's interrupt, `:seon.flow/launcher-stopped`) and resolve such a fault once none of its occurrences' processes is live; resolve by the failing operation (`:seon.error/operation`), not the outermost armed Var. Done when a regression's process-scoped fault reads resolved after its process ends, and editing an unrelated wrapper resolves nothing."
             :must-read #{seon.error/resolution seon.problems/open-faults seon.fault/fault!}
             :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/stability-sweep-2026-09-27.md"}}
 #:seon.task{:name "a-fault-notification-is-its-errors-edn-as-text"
             :kind :function
             :intent "A fault's notification message carries the error value printed as EDN text (message-tx: `:seon.message/content` (`seon.render.value/bounded-text` (value fact))). On default 2026-09-27, 33 of root's 35 unread messages were such strings, so its inbox (and the runtime trigger it wakes on) shows \"#:seon.error{:at\"…+412: the content head is timestamp and layer, never what failed. Content is for the reader: the error's message and operation as its text, with the whole record one read away through `:seon.message/about` (the signature). Done when a notified agent's inbox entry reads what failed and where within its first line, and the error value is not re-printed into the message."
             :must-read #{seon.error/message-tx}}
 #:seon.task{:name "a-distance-zero-fault-render-omits-whether-it-is-open"
             :kind :function
             :intent "A fault named in a function's related data (:seon.instrument/_fn) shows its message and occurrence count but not whether it is open or resolved (`seon.error/resolution`), so thirteen faults beside `seon.test/run` cannot be told apart from history (2026-09-28). Done when the distance-zero fault render carries its resolution."
             :must-read #{seon.error/render-ai seon.error/resolution}
             :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/profiling-and-related-data-2026-09-28.md"}}
 #:seon.task{:name "the-error-observation-pull-names-541-attributes"
             :kind :function
             :intent "`seon.error/observation-selector` names 541 attributes (every declared error extension's members), so pulling 47 error signatures costs 133 ms against 4.6 ms for the wildcard pull it replaced in `seon.problems/error-signatures` (default, armed, 2026-09-28); the wildcard read depended on every attribute, so the selector is kept for attribution. Done when an error pull costs about the wildcard's while its reads still name attributes (e.g. errors store refs and a blob, plan §3)."
             :must-read #{seon.error/observation-selector seon.problems/error-signatures}
             :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-08/task-census/evidence/health-page--RESUME.md"}}
 #:seon.task{:name "a-fixed-fault-with-an-answering-task-has-no-proof-path"
             :kind :function
             :intent "Fault 7b2cf983e1a4 (unreadable-file!, fixed by 9516842e1 + 4b29a0689 on 2026-09-28) stayed open 8 days; 13 faults open 2026-10-06. `seon.error/resolution` closes a fault whose producer digest changed ONLY when no task answers it (empty? tasks); with an answering task (every producer-task auto-created one) it needs `seon.error/proof`: a test naming the task, red on a proposing branch and green in one accepted merge proposal. A fix landed by bin/lane commit never records that, so the four faults with a changed producer digest (`my.fs/read`, `my.fs/write!`, `my.shell/run!`, `my.program/diff`) are held open by their own task, and a fault whose producer is the thrower (unreadable-file!, `seon.db/transact!`, retire-branch!) never sees a digest change when the cause is a caller or the loader (then == now for 7b2cf9). Decide what counts as proof of a fix outside the proposal flow (options in docs/research or the lane report: a green stored run of a test naming the task at current digests; a human resolve!; resolve by occurrence process scope), then derive it in `seon.error/resolution` without a second mechanism. Done when a regression writes a fault with a task, changes the producer, records the proof and reads the fault resolved, and the 7b2cf9 case resolves."
             :must-read #{seon.error/proof seon.error/resolution seon.problems/open-faults seon.task/resolution}}
 #:seon.task{:name "s1-left-metadata-readers-and-stamps-in-three-test-files"
             :kind :namespace
             :intent "Errors S1 (33fb994f2) moved the error variant from a vary-meta `:seon.error/declared-schema` stamp to the `:seon.error/type` key but missed test sites: test/seon/error/declared_identity_test.clj:14 and :30 still read the metadata, so producers-declare-the-identity-settlement-records now fails its three identity assertions; the failure helper and fixtures at test/seon/cluster/turn_test.clj:1473, 1824-1836, 2538, 2584 and test/seon/turn_loop_test.clj:328 still stamp metadata, so `seon.turn/record-attempt!` sees no declaration and `seon.error/recording` normalizes the starvation variant, losing `:seon.ai/exhausted-finish-reason` that reasoning-starvation-persists-usage-finish-and-the-named-error asserts (static finding; the phase/opening fixtures can pass while normalized). The spec's S1 rule is 'delete every vary-meta ... declared-schema' (errors.md §7). Errors slice S1b (with seon.error/a-converted-error-keeps-its-transient-type). Done when no test reads or stamps the metadata, the fixtures assert their stored variant, and the review's focused list (both review files, 'Focused checks') is green on the S1b commit. Proof: seon.error.declared-identity-test/producers-declare-the-identity-settlement-records and `seon.cluster.turn-test/reasoning-starvation-persists-usage-finish-and-the-named-error`, naming this task."
             :must-read #{seon.error/recording seon.render/declared-producers seon.turn/record-attempt!}
             :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-08/task-census/evidence/model-trial--review-s1-trial-astra-s1.md" "docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-08/task-census/evidence/model-trial--review-s1-trial-sol61-s1.md"}}
 #:seon.task{:name "error-messages-print-growing-values"
             :kind :namespace
             :intent "Error messages are built by printing values that grow with input (the offending value, every argument, a whole entity or transaction report, every moved identity, ex-message chains copied into new ex-info messages), so one refusal can carry megabytes of Seon's own text. Owner 2026-10-07: never print bulk in errors; the error map holds the value by reference (offending digest or blob) and the message names it in bounded words, the value printer shows the rest. Inventory 2026-10-07, class error-text in tmp/no-print-hash/print-sites.tsv, 56 sites: db.clj 9, fn.clj 5, schema/internal.cljc 4, test/seon/test_support.clj 4, config.clj 3, schema.clj 3, schema/admission.clj 3, test/runner.clj 3, turn.clj 3, cluster/source.clj 2, error.clj 2, render.clj 2, render/transcript.clj 2, script/dev/harness_costs.clj 1, script/operator.clj 1, batch.clj 1, cluster/agent.clj 1, effect.clj 1, fault.clj 1, problems.clj 1, sci/arm.clj 1, sci/kernel.clj 1, test.clj 1, turn/batch.clj 1. Done when no message interpolates a collection or whole value (scalars only), each site keeps its value as data, and a regression in seon.error-test refuses a write whose offending value prints over 10 MB and asserts the message is under 200 estimated tokens while :seon.error/offending-digest names the value."
             :must-read #{seon.error/recording seon.db/value-type-error seon.fn/require-committed!}
             :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-08/task-census/evidence/no-print-hash--print-sites.tsv" "docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-08/task-census/evidence/no-print-hash--notes.md"}}
 #:seon.task{:name "error-admission-is-a-second-clipper"
             :kind :namespace
             :intent "seon.error (bounded-admission, bounded-error-admission, bounded-text, bound-text, fit-fact-payload), seon.error.refusal (bounded-cost, bounded-data, chain) and seon.edit (bounded-values) each bound and clip values by their own byte caps, printing values to measure them (pr-str per fact, utf8-size of printed text): a second and third clipping system beside the value printer. Owner 2026-10-07: no random clipping in a dozen spots; real values are kept and the value printer is the only way we print. Inventory class second-clipper, 36 sites: error.clj 22, `seon.error/refusal`.clj 9, edit.clj 5. Done when errors store the whole value by reference (blob digest) with no clip, the printer alone bounds what is shown, the three bounding walks are deleted, and seon.error-test asserts an error over a 10 MB value stores its digest and the reply shows it through the printer's elision with a dig form."
             :must-read #{seon.error/fit-fact-payload seon.error.refusal/chain seon.edit/form}
             :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-08/task-census/evidence/no-print-hash--print-sites.tsv" "docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-08/task-census/evidence/no-print-hash--notes.md"}}
 #:seon.task{:name
            "a-fault-without-an-operation-is-recorded-under-normalize",
            :kind :function,
            :intent
            "`seon.error/prepare` names 'seon.error/normalize when neither the failure, the instrument data nor the boundary names an operation, so three StackOverflowError flow faults (deep-value-probe, 2026-10-07 02:08Z; two on 09-28) read as the recorder overflowing. Their producers (recursive canonical print and error-data walk) were made iterative in 77c9f5459 and 7a6878374; the misattribution remains. Done when such a fault names its boundary or a typed unknown operation, never the recorder.",
            :must-read #{seon.error/prepare},
            :evidence
            #{"docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-07/growth/growth-notes.md"}}
 #:seon.task{:name
            "an-error-render-drops-the-members-that-say-what-is-missing",
            :kind :function,
            :intent
            "`seon.test/recorded-result`'s unknown answer {`:seon.test/unknown` sym `:seon.test/next-tier` :none `:seon.error/message` ...} is shown to the agent as the bare string \"No admitted execution is recorded for this test.\": the error AI face prints its message alone, so which test is unknown and what tier would run it are dropped. Done when an error's AI render keeps its variant's own members as data beside the message, asserted on the render's data.",
            :must-read #{seon.error/render-ai},
            :evidence
            #{"docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-07/context-design/reference-kinds-notes.md"}}
 #:seon.task{:name "fault-task-closing-has-no-writer-left",
            :kind :function,
            :intent
            "Recording no longer writes a producer task, so `:seon.task/faults` is fed by no writer: `seon.task/task-resolution`'s fault branch, `my.task/open`'s fault query and `seon.error/resolution`'s task-proof branch (proof) serve only the auto tasks written before 2026-10-07 (18 'faults of <fn>' tasks on default). Triage those into authored tasks with failing tests or retire them, then delete `:seon.task/faults`, the proof branch and their tests at the errors cut. Open decision for the errors spec owner: how an untriaged recorded error resolves (today: producer digest change alone, or `seon.problems/resolve!`). Proof: the attribute and the proof branch are gone and seon.error.resolution-test asserts the remaining rules.",
            :must-read
            #{seon.error/resolution seon.task/task-resolution}}
 #:seon.task{:name "fault-window-derives-the-error-selector-when-no-error-occurred"
             :kind :function
             :intent "`seon.error/occurred-since` computes observation-selector whenever its query answers a vector, even an empty one; the selector is held per projection, so the first pass after any declaration write rederives it over the whole registry: 12-13 MB and 13.5 ms of the 94 MB pass after a defn (defn-why, 2026-10-08). Derive the selector only when the window holds an error, and hold it by the schema forms it reads (as `seon.program/program-attributes` now is), not by the projection value. Done when the pass after a defn allocates nothing in observation-selector with no errors in its window."
             :must-read #{seon.error/occurred-since seon.error/observation-selector}
             :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-08/defn-why/defn-why.md"}}
 #:seon.task{:name "commit-tx-stored-the-whole-admitted-data-edn-over-the-fitted-one"
             :kind :function
             :intent "`seon.error/prepare` returned the observation carrying the whole admitted data-edn as `:seon.error/source`, and `seon.error/commit-tx` stores the source's declared members over the fact's, so a map-sourced fault stored 300 KB inline while its fitted fact held 52 bytes (lane fault-data-edn, b233d838f). Fixed: the source keeps the data-edn the fact kept. Done when seon.error-evidence-test/a-capped-turn-fault-says-it-is-capped asserts the stored data-edn fits `:seon.config.error/max-evidence-bytes` (b233d838f). SP-1a (cards/SP-1a.md) deletes `:seon.error/data-edn` and this fix with it: the task is then done by deletion of its producer."
             :must-read #{seon.error/prepare seon.error/commit-tx}
             :evidence #{"b233d838f"}}
 #:seon.task{:name "error-notifications-to-root-are-printed-maps"
             :kind :function
             :intent "Error notifications to root are outside messages whose text is a pr-str of the error map (a second printer), delivered through :seon.config.error/escalate-to. Done when the notification carries the error's identity (signature, task, handle) as data and no printed copy."
             :must-read #{seon.error/commit-call}}
 #:seon.task{:name "a-missing-key-held-under-another-namespace-is-not-named"
             :kind :function
             :intent "An agent called (my.message/send {:seon.message/to \"x\" :seon.message/content \"hi\"}) and was refused for missing `:my.message/to` and `:my.message/content` with the fix \"Supply :my.message/to with a string.\", never told that its map holds the same names under the seon.message namespace (agent tw-probe, default 0f0e77ed8, 2026-10-09). `seon.error/explain-problem` builds that fix for a Malli missing-key problem from the path alone, though its request carries the map as :seon.error/parent. Done when the fix of a missing qualified key whose `name` the parent map holds under another namespace also names that held key (:seon.message/to in the example), and a parent holding no such key keeps the fix unchanged. Checked by `seon.error-test/a-missing-key-names-the-same-name-the-map-holds`, which calls `seon.error/explain-problem` directly."
             :must-read #{seon.error/explain-problem malli.core/explain}}
]
